omments":1,"created_at":"2026-03-10T11:17:48Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T22:16:58Z","closed_at":"2026-03-10T19:29:32Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n - Reproducible in: v4.7.dev2.official [778cf54da]\n - Not Reproducible: v4.7.dev1.official\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev2 - Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie) 13 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated Intel(R) HD Graphics 500 (APL 2) - Intel(R) Celeron(R) CPU N3350 @ 1.10GHz (2 threads) - 5.64 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nOn a laptop, using a trackpad, I've found this can lead to accidentally dragging an object rapidly across the scene, when I only intend to move things slightly.\nNeeding to now double-press F, to undo that Follow Mode each time, slows my workflow down.\nI'd like to be able to disable this new Follow Mode in the Editor Settings.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a 3D scene.\nAdd a Label3D node.\nSelect it the 3D Editor.\nMove it about the scene.\nPress F (once) to focus the Editor Camera on that selected node.\nNote you'll also now be following node too, until you press F again.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8f27221-5ee2-4458-a46c-bd5ad2932d8c","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"h